        ],
        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "T-B- severe combined immunodeficiency (SCID) is a group of rare monogenic primary immunodeficiency disorders characterized by a lack of functional peripheral T and B lymphocytes resulting in recurrent early-onset severe respiratory viral bacterial or fungal infections diarrhea and failure to thrive. Hypersensitivity to ionizing radiation is a characteristic feature of some of its sub-types."
        },
